{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.UntwistedMonodromyPrune","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.UntwistedMonodromyPrune","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UntwistedMonodromyPrune.neg_inv_eigen_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UntwistedMonodromyPrune.neg_inv_eigen_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UntwistedMonodromyPrune.lean#L46-L60","doc":"The negative Hecke eigenvalue `−q⁻¹` is not of finite order either (for `q > 1`):\nits `k`-th power has absolute value `q^{−k} < 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UntwistedMonodromyPrune.quasi_unipotent_eigen_ne_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UntwistedMonodromyPrune.quasi_unipotent_eigen_ne_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UntwistedMonodromyPrune.lean#L38-L44","doc":"Quasi-unipotence `(λ^k − 1)^m = 0` (with `m ≥ 1`) already forces `λ^k = 1` in a field,\nso a quasi-unipotent eigenvalue is never `> 1` either. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.UntwistedMonodromyPrune.finite_order_eigen_ne_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.UntwistedMonodromyPrune.finite_order_eigen_ne_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/UntwistedMonodromyPrune.lean#L30-L36","doc":"A finite-order eigenvalue is never a real number greater than one. ","signatureChunk":0}]}